-- Q4706: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8, Chapter 1, paragraph OB2, the primary objective of general-purpose financial reporting is to provide information useful to existing and potential investors, lenders, and other creditors in making resource allocation decisions. This decision-usefulness objective drives all other aspects of the Conceptual Framework.
Wrong (B): Determining taxable income is the purpose of tax accounting under the IRC, not the objective of general-purpose financial reporting under GAAP.
Wrong (C): General-purpose financial statements serve external users such as investors and creditors, not exclusively internal management.
Wrong (D): Financial reporting aims to provide decision-useful information, not to calculate liquidation value; liquidation-basis reporting applies only in specific circumstances under ASC 205-30.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4706;

