-- Q4709: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 105-10-05 and SFAC No. 6, paragraph 82, gains are defined as increases in equity from peripheral or incidental transactions of an entity, distinct from revenues or investments by owners. A land sale outside core operations fits this definition precisely.
Wrong (A): Revenue arises from an entity''s ongoing major or central operations, such as sales of goods or services, not from peripheral transactions.
Wrong (B): Expenses are decreases in equity from delivering goods or rendering services, the opposite direction from the gain described.
Wrong (C): Comprehensive income is the total change in equity from nonowner sources for a period, encompassing all revenues, expenses, gains, and losses rather than being a single element.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4709;

-- Q4711: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 105-10-05 and SFAC No. 8, paragraphs QC6-QC10, relevance means information is capable of making a difference in user decisions by possessing predictive value, confirmatory value, or both. Without the capacity to influence decisions, information lacks relevance regardless of other qualities.
Wrong (A): Information that is free from error and complete describes faithful representation under ASC 105-10-05 (QC12), a separate fundamental characteristic, not relevance.
Wrong (C): Information that can be independently verified describes verifiability (QC26), an enhancing qualitative characteristic rather than a fundamental one.
Wrong (D): Information presented in a clear and concise manner describes understandability (QC30), another enhancing characteristic, not a component of relevance.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4711;

-- Q4712: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 105-10-05 and SFAC No. 8, paragraph QC12, faithful representation requires three attributes: completeness (all necessary data included), neutrality (free from bias), and freedom from error (no mistakes in description or process). All three must be present for a faithfully represented depiction.
Wrong (A): Predictive value, confirmatory value, and materiality are components of relevance under ASC 105-10-05 (QC6-QC11), not faithful representation.
Wrong (B): Relevance is a separate fundamental characteristic, and timeliness and comparability are enhancing characteristics under ASC 105-10-05 — none are attributes of faithful representation.
Wrong (D): Verifiability, timeliness, and understandability are all enhancing qualitative characteristics under ASC 105-10-05, not components of faithful representation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4712;

-- Q4714: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8, paragraph OB7, and ASC 205-40, the going concern assumption presumes the entity will continue operating long enough to carry out its existing objectives and commitments. This assumption underlies historical cost accounting, systematic depreciation, and current/noncurrent balance sheet classification.
Wrong (B): Liquidation within 12 months is the opposite of the going concern assumption; liquidation-basis reporting under ASC 205-30 applies when liquidation is imminent.
Wrong (C): Tax-basis preparation is a special purpose framework under AU-C 800 and is unrelated to the going concern assumption about operational continuity.
Wrong (D): Distributing all earnings annually describes a specific dividend policy, not the going concern assumption, which concerns operational continuity rather than payout decisions.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4714;

